It shall be unlawful for any minor to loiter, wander, stroll, or play in or upon any public place unsupervised by a parent, guardian or other adult 21 years of age or older having the lawful care and custody of the minor and having the lawful authority to be at such places between the hours of 11:00 p.m. and 6:00 a.m.; and provided further that the provisions of this section shall not apply in the following instances:
(1) When the minor is engaged upon an emergency errand directed by his /her parent, guardian or other adult person 21 years of age or older having the lawful care and custody of the minor;
(2) When the minor is traveling directly home from a school-sponsored activity;
(3) When the minor is traveling to, or returning home from, lawful employment that makes it necessary to be in any of the above referenced places during the proscribed periods of time;
(4) When the minor is attending or traveling to or from any activity involving the exercise of First Amendment rights of free speech, freedom of assembly, or free exercise of religion; and/or engaged in a school-sponsored activity;
(5) When the minor is engaged in interstate and intrastate vehicular travel through city with parental and/or guardians consent;
(6) When the minor is on the sidewalk adjoining the property where the minor resides or on the property where the minor resides or on either side of or across the street from the property where the minor resides and the adult owner or resident of that property has given permission for the minor to be there; and
(7) When the minor is married or has been married pursuant to state law.
(Ord. of 3-24-2023, § 1)
